  "nl_text": "The rschema_0213 database is designed to manage customer information and their contracts, as well as track payment records for these contracts. The Customer table stores details about each customer, including a unique identifier (Customer_ID), their email address, name, and phone number. The Contract table represents the agreements between customers and the service provider, with each contract having a unique identifier (Contract_ID), an amount, start and end times, and a description of the service content. The Contract table is linked to the Customer table through the Customer_ID, which is a foreign key that references the Customer_ID in the Customer table, and this relationship is set up with an ON DELETE RESTRICT rule to prevent the deletion of a customer if they have active contracts. The Payment_Record table tracks payments made by customers for their contracts, with each payment having a unique identifier (Payment_ID), a contract identifier (Contract_ID) that references the Contract table, a payment amount, and a payment date. The Contract_ID in the Payment_Record table is also a foreign key that references the Contract_ID in the Contract table, and this relationship is set up with an ON DELETE CASCADE rule to automatically delete any payment records when a contract is deleted.",
  "gold_question": "A business services company manages multiple contracts, each contract has a Contract ID, Customer, Service Content, Start Time, End Time, and Contract Amount.\nCustomers have a Customer ID, Name, Phone, and Email.\nThe company needs to record the payment status of contracts, each payment must record the Payment Date and Payment Amount.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0213.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0213\nCREATE TABLE `customer` (\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`customer_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `contract` (\n  `contract_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `amount` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `start_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `end_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `service_description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`contract_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `contract_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customer` (`customer_id`) ON DELETE RESTRICT ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `payment_record` (\n  `payment_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `contract_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `payment_amount` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `payment_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`payment_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `payment_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`contract_id`) REFERENCES `contract` (`contract_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
